            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="0710" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5041/25: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-09T10:00:00-00:44">July 9, 1943—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. President Barclay informs me labor law is experimental and subject to
                    change. He intimates that growing out of conversations at Akron, there is a
                    possibility of legislature at next session modifying provision regarding
                    agricultural labor.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
